a ton of you are interested in valor n't  and we're giving you the basic rundown  so you can understand what this game is  all about valor n't is a character based  tactical shooter by Riot Games the folks  that make team fight tactics and of  course League of Legends it combines  aspects of Counter Strike global  Offensive Rainbow six siege and  overwatch and is currently running a  closed beta the heroes environment are  called agents and there are five to  start off with and an additional five to  unlock each agent in the beta fills a  role initiators disrupt choke points in  order to let their team get into  contested spaces duelists are multi-role  fighters that focus on frags and  aggressive pushing sentinels help to  fortify locations such as sites where  you can plant the spike controllers have  area-denial attacks designed to split up  combat spaces in order to divide and  conquer  time-to-kill is fast in this game so  you'll have a small window to react and  get abilities off than in a game like  overwatch you'll also probably be  familiar with some of these abilities  from other games such as orbital strikes  elemental walls and spy cameras the  current mode in the beta pits teams of  five against each other until one team  reaches 13 wins your team will be  assigned to either defend or attack the  objective for the first 12 rounds before  switching sides you win a round either  by wiping out the enemy team or by  planting the spike and guarding it until  it detonates  there's a csgo style buying phase at the  start of each round where you can  purchase weapons armor and charges for  your agents unique abilities in the  beats at the economy is pretty forgiving  with a loss netting you 1,900 points a  win 3,000 points and kills around 200  each that means you'll be stocked with  low to mid tier weapons consistently  presuming you don't overspend on the  more expensive weapons in our experience  some of the higher level sniper rifles  can begin to dominate but the game is  still in its early stages so the meta is  still developing it's important to  recognize the benefit of certain tactics  and systems for example moving slowly  will cancel out the sound of your  footsteps and is a must make sure you  reserve Sprint for when you're already  engaged certain guns such as rifles and  SMGs rifles will allow aiming down  sights with different damage numbers  depending on how you shoot another thing  to keep in mind is how each agents  ultimate ability charges if you die in a  round win or lose you will gain one alt  point although how many points you need  before you use your alt varies by agent  other ways you gain out points involve  capturing the silver or black orbs that  spawn in-game planting or defusing the  spiked bomb and getting kills the maps  we've seen so far tend to have longer  sightlines on the outer edges and close  to medium engagements at the center  remaining delete no.1 pain target there  are plenty of choke points for teams to  pile up plenty of lanes for agents with  a sniper rifle to lock down and many  tight corners to keep eyes on the number  of bomb sites can vary per map the rules  stay the same once a team finds a spike  the other must diffuse or lose even if  they wipe the defending team Valery also  comes with a pretty handy training area  where you can try every weapon and even  raise or lower mouse sensitivity in game  we haven't found any controller support  yet but for those brushing up on their  mouse and keyboard twitch skills the  training area is a must especially when  the game rewards headshots significantly  more than body shots there is also a  microtransaction area already available  to sell you skins and buddies you can  also earn buddies sprays cards titles  and some gunskins by leveling agent  contracts although the microtransaction  store will have exclusive goodies we'll  have plenty more tips and excellent  content soon as we cover this much hyped  game so definitely stay tuned and check  out our other video guides and feature  articles valor --nt is scheduled to  release this summer 2020 last player  standing  attackers win
 

